.TH PAPERSPIDER-CLI 1 "2026-11-23" "PaperSpider 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
paperspider-cli \- search, download, and export conference papers from a local PaperSpider library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paperspider-cli
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fICOMMAND OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B paperspider-cli
works on the conference paper library created by the PaperSpider desktop
application.
It runs directly and exits after one command, so no background server is
needed.
.PP
The library stores each conference year as a SQLite database with downloaded
PDF and BibTeX files.
Commands can list conferences and datasets, fetch a paper list, search papers,
read or download abstracts, download PDFs and BibTeX, and export metadata.
.PP
Human-readable data is written to standard output.
Progress summaries and failures are written to standard error.
Use
.B \-\-json
to make every command emit a single JSON document on standard output.
.PP
Commands that fetch or download from the internet are \fBadd\fR,
\fBdownload\-abstracts\fR, \fBdownload\-pdfs\fR, \fBdownload\-bibtex\fR,
\fBexport\fR with \fB\-\-format bibtex\fR, and \fBshow\fR with
\fB\-\-fetch\fR.
All other operations read only the local library.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Global options may appear before or after the command name.
.TP
.BI \-\-base\-dir " DIR"
Use
.I DIR
as the storage folder.
If omitted, the value of
.B PAPERSPIDER_BASE_DIR
is used, then the folder saved by the desktop application, then
.IR ~/PaperSpider .
.TP
.BI \-\-delay\-ms " MS"
Wait
.I MS
milliseconds between web requests.
The default is
.BR 100 .
Valid values are 0 to 10000.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print machine-readable JSON instead of text.
For
.BR export ,
the JSON document contains the export content together with its format,
paper count, path, and failures.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a command summary and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS conferences
.B paperspider-cli conferences
[\fB\-\-query\fR \fITEXT\fR]
.PP
List conference adapters that can fetch paper lists.
The output has one line per conference:
.IP
.EX
SLUG<TAB>NAME
.EE
.TP
.BI \-\-query " TEXT"
Match
.I TEXT
case-insensitively against conference names and slugs.
.SS datasets
.B paperspider-cli datasets
.PP
List conference and year datasets under the base folder.
Each line contains the conference slug, year, paper count, and path relative to
the base folder:
.IP
.EX
CONF<TAB>YEAR<TAB>PAPERS<TAB>PATH
.EE
.PP
A dataset exists after
.B add
has fetched its paper list.
.SS add
.B paperspider-cli add
.I CONF YEAR
.PP
Fetch the paper list for a supported conference and year from the web and
store it locally.
An existing dataset is refreshed and paper metadata already downloaded is
preserved.
Requires network access.
.PP
.I YEAR
must be between 1980 and 2100.
The command prints the number of fetched papers, the stored total, and the
dataset path.
.SS search
.B paperspider-cli search
[\fB\-\-conf\fR \fICONF\fR] [\fB\-\-year\fR \fIYEAR\fR]
[\fB\-\-query\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-\-title\fR \fITEXT\fR]
[\fB\-\-author\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-\-keyword\fR \fITEXT\fR]
[\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-offset\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-abstract\fR]
.PP
Search papers stored in the local library.
Omit both
.B \-\-conf
and
.B \-\-year
to search every local dataset.
Omit only one of them to search all years of a conference or all conferences
for a year.
.PP
Matching papers are sorted by conference, newest year first, then title.
Each text result contains the paper id and title, a metadata line, and the
locally stored files.
.TP
.BI \-\-conf " CONF"
Restrict the search to one conference slug.
.TP
.BI \-\-year " YEAR"
Restrict the search to one conference year.
.TP
.BI \-\-query " TEXT"
Free text matched case-insensitively against title, category, authors,
abstract, and keywords.
Every whitespace-separated term must match.
.TP
.BI \-\-title " TEXT"
Keep papers whose title contains
.IR TEXT .
.TP
.BI \-\-author " TEXT"
Keep papers whose authors contain
.IR TEXT .
.TP
.BI \-\-keyword " TEXT"
Keep papers whose keywords or abstract contain
.IR TEXT .
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " N"
Return at most
.I N
papers.
The default is 20; the maximum is 200.
.TP
.BI \-\-offset " N"
Skip the first
.I N
matches.
The default is 0.
.TP
.B \-\-abstract
Include the full abstract of each returned paper.
.SS show
.B paperspider-cli show
.I CONF YEAR PAPER_ID
[\fB\-\-fetch\fR] [\fB\-\-bibtex\fR]
.PP
Show title, id, conference, category, authors, keywords, URLs, local file
paths, and abstract for one paper.
.TP
.B \-\-fetch
Refresh the abstract, authors, PDF URL, and BibTeX from the conference site and
store the result.
Requires network access.
.TP
.B \-\-bibtex
Print the cached BibTeX entry when available.
.SS download\-abstracts
.B paperspider-cli download\-abstracts
.I CONF YEAR PAPER_ID
[\fIPAPER_ID\fR ...]
.PP
Fetch missing abstracts and related metadata for one to 200 papers and store
them locally.
Papers that already have an abstract are skipped.
Each downloaded abstract is printed.
Requires network access.
The exit status is 1 when any paper fails.
.SS download\-pdfs
.B paperspider-cli download\-pdfs
.I CONF YEAR PAPER_ID
[\fIPAPER_ID\fR ...]
.PP
Download PDFs for one to 200 papers into the dataset
.B pdf/
folder.
Papers whose PDF file already exists are skipped.
Each downloaded file is printed as:
.IP
.EX
PAPER_ID<TAB>PATH
.EE
.PP
Requires network access.
The exit status is 1 when any paper fails.
.SS download\-bibtex
.B paperspider-cli download\-bibtex
.I CONF YEAR PAPER_ID
[\fIPAPER_ID\fR ...]
.PP
Download BibTeX for one to 200 papers into the dataset
.B bib/
folder and cache the entries in the local database.
Each file is printed as:
.IP
.EX
PAPER_ID<TAB>PATH
.EE
.PP
Requires network access for entries that are not already cached.
The exit status is 1 when any paper fails.
.SS export
.B paperspider-cli export
.I CONF YEAR
[\fIPAPER_ID\fR ...]
[\fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMAT\fR] [\fB\-\-no-title\fR]
[\fB\-\-no-authors\fR] [\fB\-\-abstract\fR] [\fB\-\-save\fR]
[\fB\-\-filename\fR \fINAME\fR]
.PP
Export selected papers, or every paper in the dataset when no paper ids are
given.
The export content is written to standard output.
When
.B \-\-save
is used, a copy is also written under the dataset
.B exports/
folder and its path is printed to standard error.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
Choose
.BR csv ,
.BR json ,
.BR txt ,
or
.BR bibtex .
The default is
.BR csv .
.B csv
and
.B json
contain the selected fields.
.B txt
writes one title per line.
.B bibtex
concatenates BibTeX entries and fetches missing entries from the web.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-title
Omit titles from
.B csv
and
.B json
output.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-authors
Omit authors from
.B csv
and
.B json
output.
.TP
.B \-\-abstract
Include abstracts in
.B csv
and
.B json
output.
.TP
.B \-\-save
Also write the export to the dataset
.B exports/
folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-filename " NAME"
Base file name for
.BR \-\-save .
The format extension is added automatically.
Unsafe characters are removed.
.PP
The exit status is 1 when
.B \-\-format bibtex
cannot retrieve an entry for one or more papers.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PAPERSPIDER_BASE_DIR
Storage folder used when
.B \-\-base\-dir
is not given.
If it is also unset, the folder saved by the PaperSpider desktop application is
used, followed by
.IR ~/PaperSpider .
.TP
.B PAPERSPIDER_REQUEST_DELAY_MS
Delay between web requests in milliseconds.
The default is 100.
Integer values are clamped to the range 0 to 10000; invalid values use the
default.
The
.B \-\-delay\-ms
option overrides this value.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <base>/<conf>/<year>/papers.sqlite
Paper metadata, abstracts, and file state for one conference year.
.TP
.I <base>/<conf>/<year>/pdf/
Downloaded PDF files.
.TP
.I <base>/<conf>/<year>/bib/
Downloaded BibTeX files.
.TP
.I <base>/<conf>/<year>/exports/
Files written by
.BR "export \-\-save" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, or a batch command completed with per-paper failures.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.TP
.B 130
The command was interrupted.
.SH EXAMPLES
List available conferences and local datasets:
.PP
.nf
.RS
paperspider-cli conferences
paperspider-cli datasets
.RE
.fi
.PP
Fetch a conference year:
.PP
.nf
.RS
paperspider-cli add neurips 2024
.RE
.fi
.PP
Search one dataset or the whole library:
.PP
.nf
.RS
paperspider-cli search \-\-conf neurips \-\-year 2024 \-\-query diffusion
paperspider-cli search \-\-year 2024 \-\-author "Hinton" \-\-json
paperspider-cli search \-\-conf iclr \-\-year 2025 \-\-limit 50 \-\-abstract
.RE
.fi
.PP
Read one paper and refresh its metadata:
.PP
.nf
.RS
paperspider-cli show neurips 2024 PAPER_ID
paperspider-cli show neurips 2024 PAPER_ID \-\-fetch \-\-bibtex
.RE
.fi
.PP
Download abstracts, PDFs, and BibTeX:
.PP
.nf
.RS
paperspider-cli download\-abstracts neurips 2024 PAPER_ID
paperspider-cli download\-pdfs neurips 2024 PAPER_ID1 PAPER_ID2
paperspider-cli download\-bibtex neurips 2024 PAPER_ID1 PAPER_ID2
.RE
.fi
.PP
Export metadata or BibTeX:
.PP
.nf
.RS
paperspider-cli export neurips 2024 \-\-format json \-\-abstract
paperspider-cli export neurips 2024 \-\-format bibtex \-\-save \-\-filename nips24
paperspider-cli export iclr 2025 PAPER_ID1 PAPER_ID2 \-\-format csv > papers.csv
.RE
.fi
.PP
Use a different library folder:
.PP
.nf
.RS
paperspider-cli \-\-base-dir ~/papers search \-\-query transformer
PAPERSPIDER_BASE_DIR=~/papers paperspider-cli datasets
.RE
.fi
.SH NOTES
The Python package installs this page as
.I share/man/man1/paperspider-cli.1
under its installation prefix.
If that location is on the manual page path, read it with:
.PP
.nf
.RS
man paperspider-cli
.RE
.fi
.PP
From a source checkout without installation, view it with:
.PP
.nf
.RS
man ./man/paperspider-cli.1
.RE
.fi
.PP
On systems where
.B man
does not accept a path, use
.BR "man \-l" .
To add the page to a user man path:
.PP
.nf
.RS
mkdir -p ~/.local/share/man/man1
install \-m 644 man/paperspider-cli.1 ~/.local/share/man/man1/
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The PaperSpider desktop application, started with \fBpaperspider\fR, and the
project guides
.I README.md
and
.IR docs/en.md .